---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
---

<Base
  title="Legal — Aerial"
  description="License, attribution, and privacy disclosures for Aerial."
>
  <section class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-6 pt-24 pb-32 prose prose-invert">
    <p class="text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-widest text-aerial-accent !mb-2 !mt-0">
      Legal
    </p>
    <h1 class="!mt-3 text-4xl md:text-5xl !font-bold tracking-tight text-aerial-text">
      License and attribution.
    </h1>

    <h2 class="text-aerial-text">Aerial license</h2>
    <p class="text-aerial-text-muted">
      Aerial is open-source software, released under the
      <a href="https://github.com/AerialScreensaver/Aerial/blob/main/LICENSE" class="text-aerial-link">
        MIT license
      </a>. © Guillaume Louel and contributors. The full license text is in the source
      repository.
    </p>

    <h2 class="text-aerial-text">Apple's videos</h2>
    <p class="text-aerial-text-muted">
      The aerial videos from macOS and tvOS are produced by Apple. Aerial downloads them from
      Apple's content delivery network onto your Mac, the same way macOS itself does. It does not
      host, mirror or redistribute them.
    </p>

    <h2 class="text-aerial-text">Expansions</h2>
    <p class="text-aerial-text-muted">
      Every expansion pack declares its own license in its manifest, and nothing is installed
      unless you choose to. The free Community packs by Joshua Michaels &amp; Hal Bergman are
      shared under the terms at
      <a href="https://jetsoncreative.com/aeriallicense" class="text-aerial-link">
        jetsoncreative.com/aeriallicense
      </a>. Their paid packs come with their own terms, available where you buy them.
    </p>

    <h2 class="text-aerial-text">Privacy</h2>
    <p class="text-aerial-text-muted">
      Aerial has no telemetry, no analytics and no crash reporting of any kind. There is no
      Aerial server, and nothing identifies you in the requests it makes. Out of the box it talks
      to Apple's content delivery network to download videos, and to this site (GitHub Pages) for
      update checks, the expansions catalog and video thumbnails.
    </p>
    <p class="text-aerial-text-muted">
      Some optional features reach other services when you turn them on: the weather overlay
      queries OpenWeather, YouTube live feeds go through yt-dlp to YouTube, camera feeds connect
      to whatever address you gave them, and automatic location uses Apple's Location Services.
      Each of those has its own privacy policy, which I'd encourage you to read.
    </p>

    <h2 class="text-aerial-text">Trademarks</h2>
    <p class="text-aerial-text-muted">
      Apple, macOS, tvOS, Apple TV and Mac are trademarks of Apple Inc., registered in the U.S.
      and other countries. Aerial is a third-party project with no affiliation to Apple.
    </p>

    <h2 class="text-aerial-text">Thanks</h2>
    <p class="text-aerial-text-muted">
      Aerial is built on the work of others:
      <a href="https://sparkle-project.org/" class="text-aerial-link">Sparkle</a> for updates,
      created by Andy Matuschak and kept alive since by Kornel Lesiński and, today, Mayur
      Pawashe (Zorg);
      <a href="https://github.com/sindresorhus/KeyboardShortcuts" class="text-aerial-link">KeyboardShortcuts</a>
      by Sindre Sorhus for the global hotkeys,
      <a href="https://github.com/ungive/mediaremote-adapter" class="text-aerial-link">mediaremote-adapter</a>
      by Jonas van den Berg (BSD 3-Clause) for the music overlay, and
      <a href="https://github.com/AerialScreensaver/PaperSaver" class="text-aerial-link">PaperSaver</a>
      for talking to the macOS wallpaper system. Live feeds optionally rely on
      <a href="https://ffmpeg.org/" class="text-aerial-link">ffmpeg</a> and
      <a href="https://github.com/yt-dlp/yt-dlp" class="text-aerial-link">yt-dlp</a>, which you
      install yourself.
    </p>
    <p class="text-aerial-text-muted">
      John Coates started the project in 2015. The
      <a href="https://github.com/JohnCoates/Aerial" class="text-aerial-link">original repository</a>
      keeps the early history.
    </p>
  </section>
</Base>
